<v Ira Glass>什么？

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:01.140
<v Alan Pean>Yeah.
<v Alan Pean>是的。

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:11.490
<v Ira Glass>I'm just trying to picture this. So you're in a suburban apartment complex. You're on the third floor. You're on a balcony. You're holding on to it. You let go. And you're able to drop one floor down and catch--
<v Ira Glass>我只是在尝试想象这个画面。所以你在一个郊区的公寓大楼里。你在三楼。你在阳台上。你抓着它。你松手了。你能往下掉一层楼并抓住——

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:12.940
<v Alan Pean>Catch myself.
<v Alan Pean>抓住自己。

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:14.390
<v Ira Glass>And not break your arms?
<v Ira Glass>而且没摔断胳膊？

00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:23.920
<v Alan Pean>Nothing happened. Yeah. All my muscles must have been-- you're like high. You're just-- adrenaline pumping. That's what I'm trying to say, like an adrenaline high, and it's just--
<v Alan Pean>什么事都没发生。是的。我所有的肌肉一定都——就像你在亢奋中。你只是——肾上腺素飙升。这就是我想说的，就像肾上腺素带来的快感，它只是——

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:24.620
<v Ira Glass>OK, then?
<v Ira Glass>好吧，然后呢？

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:31.630
<v Alan Pean>So then after that, I catch myself on the second story. And I look down. And I keep telling myself, just remember your training. You trained for this.
<v Alan Pean>在那之后，我抓住了二楼。我往下看。我一直告诉自己，记住你的训练。你为此训练过。

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:33.900
<v Ira Glass>And that refers to nothing, right?
<v Ira Glass>那指的不是什么吧，对吗？

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:42.020
<v Alan Pean>What, my football training? No, I don't know. I never trained for anything. So I'm just here, like, remember your training. You know, so--
<v Alan Pean>什么，我的足球训练？不，我不知道。我从来没接受过任何训练。所以我只是在那儿，心想，记住你的训练。你知道，所以——

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:43.630
<v Ira Glass>Yeah.
<v Ira Glass>是的。

00:11:43.630 --> 00:12:03.060
<v Alan Pean>And I look down, and there's these two AC units down there. And I basically, from the second story to the AC units, I do a parkour stunt, like jump off of it and then jump onto the sidewalk. And I start running.
<v Alan Pean>我往下看，下面有两台空调外机。我基本上从二楼跳到空调外机上，做了一个跑酷特技，像跳下去然后跳到人行道上。然后我开始跑。

00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:21.370
<v Ira Glass>OK, I know it's a cliche, but the mind, it is powerful. By the way, this story about jumping down the balcony seems to be completely true. We checked with the property manager of the building. And for a bunch of reasons that I won't bore you with here, the way Alan's apartment was locked, the only way he could have gotten out was off the balcony.
<v Ira Glass>好吧，我知道这是老生常谈，但思维，它确实强大。顺便说一句，这个关于跳下阳台的故事似乎完全是真的。我们和楼管核实过了。出于一些我不会在这里让你感到无聊的原因，艾伦公寓的锁法导致他唯一的出路就是阳台。

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:39.140
<v Ira Glass>So after Alan action-heroes his way down the balcony, he makes his way to his car-- not a direct path, of course. Too dangerous. Evasive maneuvers, under cover of night. He believes that he called in a drone strike using Google Maps, and any second the whole apartment complex is going to be blown up. So he's racing against the clock.
<v Ira Glass>所以艾伦像动作英雄一样从阳台下来后，他朝自己的车走去——当然不是直接走过去。太危险了。采取规避机动，在夜色的掩护下。他相信他利用谷歌地图呼叫了无人机空袭，随时整栋公寓大楼都要被炸平。所以他在与时间赛跑。

00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:54.190
<v Ira Glass>And it's interesting. I didn't know what I thought a delusion would be like. I thought it might be like a hallucination or something. It might make no sense when you look at it later. But in this case, it's a totally logical story with consistent details, like a movie or a video game.
<v Ira Glass>这很有趣。我不知道我以为妄想会是什么样子。我以为可能就像幻觉什么的。当你事后看它时，它可能毫无意义。但在这种情况下，它是一个完全合乎逻辑的故事，细节前后一致，就像电影或电子游戏一样。

00:12:54.190 --> 00:12:57.140
<v Alan Pean>I'm kind of jogging, running.
<v Alan Pean>我当时大概在慢跑、奔跑。

00:12:57.140 --> 00:12:59.680
<v Ira Glass>And you're full-on delusion? You're not ever coming to--
<v Ira Glass>你完全处于妄想中？你从来没有清醒过来——

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:16.650
<v Alan Pean>Yeah. At this point, I do believe I'm a bionic person. I'm a cyborg. I'm a secret agent on a mission to break himself out from behind enemy lines. So I get in my car, and I basically peel out. And I get to the gate.
<v Alan Pean>是的。此时，我确实相信我是一个仿生人。我是半机械人。我是执行秘密任务的特工，要从敌后冲出来。所以我上了车，基本上猛冲出去。我到了大门口。

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:18.620
<v Ira Glass>The gate of your suburban apartment--
<v Ira Glass>你郊区公寓的门——

00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:29.530
<v Alan Pean>Apartment complex. And I'm like, why isn't the gate opening? They locked it. They locked it, of course. You know, so I just rammed the gate open.
<v Alan Pean>公寓大楼。我心想，为什么门不开？他们锁上了。当然，他们锁上了。你知道，所以我直接把门撞开了。

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:30.800
<v Ira Glass>You rammed the gate with your car?
<v Ira Glass>你开车撞了门？

00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:44.280
<v Alan Pean>That's right. Boom, it opens. Get out. Take a left, and there I am. I'm driving. I'm driving, and I'm having these thoughts, like, that place is about to explode.
<v Alan Pean>没错。轰，门开了。出去。左转，我就在那里。我在开车。我开着车，脑子里有这些想法，比如，那个地方马上要爆炸了。

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:58.230
<v Alan Pean>However, as I'm driving, I tell myself, you were supposed to go somewhere before. Where's the rendezvous point? And it's at the hospital. It's at the hospital that you're supposed to go to. That's where the good guys are.
<v Alan Pean>然而，开车时，我告诉自己，你本来是要去别的地方的。集合点在哪里？是在医院。你要去的是医院。好人都在那里。

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:03.690
<v Ira Glass>But then he has a moment. He remembered, he and his dad had talked about going to the hospital for a different reason.
<v Ira Glass>但随后他有了一瞬间的清醒。他记得他和父亲谈过因为别的原因去医院。

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:13.140
<v Alan Pean>I had a moment of clarity. I need my medication. I need that. It's like-- it's Geodon. It's an anti-psychotic.
<v Alan Pean>我有了一瞬间的清醒。我需要我的药。我需要那个。它就像——是Geodon。它是一种抗精神病药。

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:25.080
<v Ira Glass>Then the delusion kicks back in. So he's driving, looking for a hospital. Remember, he's just moved to town that month. And he sees St. Joseph Medical Center, Houston's oldest hospital, and the only one downtown.
<v Ira Glass>然后妄想再次占了上风。所以他在开车，寻找医院。记住，他那个月刚搬到城里。他看到了圣约瑟夫医学中心，休斯顿最古老的医院，也是市中心唯一的医院。

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:37.180
<v Alan Pean>It's like I just lost control of the car. I don't really remember-- for me, it was like I was in the car, and the next thing I know, the car has crashed, and I'm falling out.
<v Alan Pean>就像我失去了对车的控制。我真的不记得——对我来说，感觉就像我在车里，接下来我知道的就是，车撞了，我从车里跌了出来。

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:39.210
<v Ira Glass>That's it? That's all you remember of the accident?
<v Ira Glass>就是这样？关于事故你只记得这些？

